  "features": [
    "VM lifecycle records actual engine creation, environment setup, bootstrap completion, first loop entry and exit relative to performance origin.",
    "Live timing getters expose measured milestones and idle time; v8Start is the compatibility field for Home JSC startup and nodeStart/startTime use the actual VM performance origin.",
    "PerformanceNodeTiming inherits directly from PerformanceEntry, preserving getters and serialization rather than losing its prototype through toClass.",
    "Natural and explicit process exit record the exit milestone before callbacks."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "The initial native regression exposed inherited PerformanceEntry brand errors after toClass discarded the timing prototype; the failed result remains without passing credit.",
    "Three queued runs refused disk admission; obsolete task executables were removed after builds/tests were terminal and final scopes reran with guards unchanged.",
    "Darwin arm64 main-process timing paths are verified; wider standalone/Bake/worker milestone behavior, Windows libuv idle measurement and Linux execution remain unverified.",
    "Full resource/observer behavior, the earlier ICU contradiction #872, complete Bun suite, remaining native/API ownership and Release/ASAN/all-platform verification remain open under #869 and #66.",
    "Pickier reports no errors and one quote-style warning in the existing mixed-style performance module."
  ],
